WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:04.709
- Home for me, first of
all, is a peace of mind,

00:00:04.709 --> 00:00:08.200
where you come home
and you're always safe.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.451
That's what home means to me,
especially for my children.

00:00:11.451 --> 00:00:13.611
Before I moved into this
home six months ago,

00:00:13.611 --> 00:00:15.109
I was livin' in the shelter.

00:00:15.109 --> 00:00:19.109
To get my own home, it
was just breathtaking.

00:00:19.109 --> 00:00:21.615
But there was nothin' in it.

00:00:21.615 --> 00:00:24.032
(soft music)

00:00:27.278 --> 00:00:30.928
- I'm Kristen Suhy and I'm
a designer at Humble Design.

00:00:30.928 --> 00:00:34.193
Everything in this warehouse
you see is donated.

00:00:34.193 --> 00:00:36.684
We work with homeless and
domestic abuse shelters

00:00:36.684 --> 00:00:37.658
with families that are moving

00:00:37.658 --> 00:00:40.204
out of those shelters and into homes.

00:00:40.204 --> 00:00:41.741
And a lot of times they have nothing

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:42.913
but the clothes on their back.

00:00:42.913 --> 00:00:44.113
That's where we step in

00:00:44.113 --> 00:00:46.044
and we provide the furniture for them,

00:00:46.044 --> 00:00:48.100
but then we also go back and decorate

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.244
and provide like those little details

00:00:50.244 --> 00:00:53.513
that make your house a home
and makes it your home.

00:00:53.513 --> 00:00:55.964
Without our help, about 46%

00:00:55.964 --> 00:00:58.941
of families coming out of
the shelter go right back in.

00:00:58.941 --> 00:01:03.452
With our help, that statistic
goes down to one percent.

00:01:03.452 --> 00:01:07.713
- I'm a direct care worker
and I work with older elder people.

00:01:07.713 --> 00:01:09.335
Before I lived in the shelter

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.052
the boyfriend that I was living with

00:01:11.052 --> 00:01:15.375
was emotionally and
physically abusive to me.

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:16.935
One day I woke up and I just said

00:01:16.935 --> 00:01:19.352
I wasn't takin' that anymore.

00:01:21.342 --> 00:01:22.972
- Today we met with Danyle

00:01:22.972 --> 00:01:25.804
and we just talked with her a little bit,

00:01:25.804 --> 00:01:27.341
found out about her back story.

00:01:27.341 --> 00:01:28.898
It sounds like she has
come out of the shelter

00:01:28.898 --> 00:01:32.300
and now has been in a house
with basically no furniture.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:36.467
She has a few pieces but no
beds, no chairs, no table.

00:01:37.924 --> 00:01:39.953
So we talked with her a little bit

00:01:39.953 --> 00:01:41.492
about what she wants in her home.

00:01:41.492 --> 00:01:44.233
We went to the home and
we took measurements,

00:01:44.233 --> 00:01:46.285
and just walked through each room.

00:01:46.285 --> 00:01:47.241
About, a bigger table?

00:01:47.241 --> 00:01:49.484
- What dinner looks at my house now,

00:01:49.484 --> 00:01:52.037
we all sit together but
we sit on the floor.

00:01:52.037 --> 00:01:56.696
The priorities was to have
silverware, bowls and spoons,

00:01:56.696 --> 00:01:58.597
stuff, things for us to eat out of.

00:01:58.597 --> 00:02:01.078
And bedding to put on the floor for us

00:02:01.078 --> 00:02:03.067
'cause we didn't have beds.

00:02:03.067 --> 00:02:05.365
- When I first started
here, I didn't realize

00:02:05.365 --> 00:02:07.427
that people were living this way.

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:11.166
When you walk into a home
that is completely empty

00:02:11.166 --> 00:02:12.368
and families are living there

00:02:12.368 --> 00:02:15.234
and have lived there for
months, it's shocking,

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:17.734
because you don't think of it.

00:02:19.867 --> 00:02:22.525
But on that Friday when we reveal a house,

00:02:22.525 --> 00:02:26.086
I just love the energy from our volunteers

00:02:26.086 --> 00:02:30.253
to the families that are
getting these, you know, new homes, really.

00:02:31.507 --> 00:02:33.146
I just, I can't get enough of that feeling

00:02:33.146 --> 00:02:36.979
and that's why I have
stayed here for so long.

00:02:38.465 --> 00:02:40.215
- I know my kids are gonna be amazed

00:02:40.215 --> 00:02:41.805
'cause I haven't really
told them what's goin' on,

00:02:41.805 --> 00:02:43.366
I just told them they
was gettin' some beds.

00:02:43.366 --> 00:02:45.107
So they don't even know
that the whole house

00:02:45.107 --> 00:02:46.455
is gonna be done.

00:02:46.455 --> 00:02:49.533
So I know they're gonna
be astounded, happy.

00:02:49.533 --> 00:02:51.866
It just makes me very happy.

00:02:52.982 --> 00:02:54.382
Oh,

00:02:54.382 --> 00:02:55.215
wow.

00:02:56.152 --> 00:02:57.291
- Ooh.

00:02:57.291 --> 00:03:00.624
(laughing)
- Oh my God!

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:04.188
- It's like a magazine.

00:03:04.188 --> 00:03:07.699
Went from zero to a miracle. (laughing)

00:03:07.699 --> 00:03:11.281
I love y'all for this,
I mean, this is amazing.

00:03:11.281 --> 00:03:12.651
This is just happiness to me,

00:03:12.651 --> 00:03:14.251
to be able to walk into a home

00:03:14.251 --> 00:03:16.251
and have your friends and family there

00:03:16.251 --> 00:03:19.539
and you're able to just
show them comfort and joy.

00:03:19.539 --> 00:03:20.931
That means a lot to me.

00:03:20.931 --> 00:03:22.748
And I hope that one day I can give back,

00:03:22.748 --> 00:03:24.910
just what was given to me.

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:27.577
(upbeat music)

